rature","title":"Wisdom Literature*"}],"dictionaryWords":[],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":["Understanding Job"],"sourceClass":"theme-title","t":"h"},{"c":["For as long as people have read Job’s story, they have struggled with the tension between the positive and negative aspects of Job’s character. The book’s approval of Job in the opening prologue is unequivocal (",{"href":"?bref=Job.1.1","r":"Job.1.1","rawR":"Job.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.1.1","value":"Job.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:1"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Job.1.8","r":"Job.1.8","rawR":"Job.1.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.1.8","value":"Job.1.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.2.3","r":"Job.2.3","rawR":"Job.2.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.2.3","value":"Job.2.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:3"},"), yet we later hear God interrogate Job: “Who is this that questions my wisdom with such ignorant words?” (",{"href":"?bref=Job.38.2","r":"Job.38.2","rawR":"Job.38.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.38.2","value":"Job.38.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"38:2"},"). “Will you discredit my justice and condemn me just to prove you are right?” (",{"href":"?bref=Job.40.8","r":"Job.40.8","rawR":"Job.40.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.40.8","value":"Job.40.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"40:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"theme-body-fl","t":"p"},{"c":["God’s questions have led various interpreters to accuse Job of talking too much and even of confusing God’s work with the work of Satan. Some contemporary interpretations side with Job’s counselors in blaming Job for his suffering. Still others follow Eliphaz (",{"href":"?bref=Job.5.17-27","r":"Job.5.17-27","rawR":"Job.5.17-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.5.17-27","value":"Job.5.17-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:17-27"},") and Elihu (",{"href":"?bref=Job.33.15-33","r":"Job.33.15-33","rawR":"Job.33.15-33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.33.15-33","value":"Job.33.15-33"}],"t":"ref","v":"33:15-33"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.36.7-17","r":"Job.36.7-17","rawR":"Job.36.7-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.36.7-17","value":"Job.36.7-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"36:7-17"},") in arguing that Job’s suffering was God’s loving and sanctifying chastisement. Even the faithful are not exempt from such discipline (",{"href":"?bref=Heb.12.6-12","r":"Heb.12.6-12","rawR":"Heb.12.6-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.12.6-12","value":"Heb.12.6-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 12:6-12"},"; see ",{"href":"?bref=Pr.3.11-12","r":"Pr.3.11-12","rawR":"Pr.3.11-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.3.11-12","value":"Pr.3.11-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prov 3:11-12"},"), but this explanation flies in the face of the rationale given in the book’s opening verses."],"sourceClass":"theme-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Job suffered because God wanted to prove Job’s integrity to Satan. God’s own judgment of Job’s life was positive from start to finish (",{"href":"?bref=Job.1.1","r":"Job.1.1","rawR":"Job.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.1.1","value":"Job.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Job 1:1"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Job.1.8","r":"Job.1.8","rawR":"Job.1.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.1.8","value":"Job.1.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.2.3","r":"Job.2.3","rawR":"Job.2.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.2.3","value":"Job.2.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.42.7","r":"Job.42.7","rawR":"Job.42.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.42.7","value":"Job.42.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:7"},"). This perspective carries through to the New Testament, where Job is an example of endurance that we should imitate (",{"href":"?bref=Jas.5.11","r":"Jas.5.11","rawR":"Jas.5.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jas.5.11","value":"Jas.5.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jas 5:11"},")."],"sourceClass":"theme-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Job’s reactions are normal. He does not stand like a rock in reverent stoicism as though he were unaffected by his trials. Neither does he trumpet heroic defiance of his troubles, as though they could never get him down. He reacts in a natural human way. Job rages, protests, moans, and vacillates between confidence and despair, but he never gives up. He does not curse God, and he does not make a false confession of guilt in the hope that God will then let up on him. Although Job cannot understand his situation, he knows that his answer will be found in God (",{"href":"?bref=Job.19.25-27","r":"Job.19.25-27","rawR":"Job.19.25-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.19.25-27","value":"Job.19.25-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Job 19:25-27"},")."],"sourceClass":"theme-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Passages for Further Study"],"sourceClass":"theme-refs-title","t":"h"},{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Job.1.1","r":"Job.1.1","rawR":"Job.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.1.1","value":"Job.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Job 1:1"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Job.1.8","r":"Job.1.8","rawR":"Job.1.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.1.8","value":"Job.1.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.2.3","r":"Job.2.3","rawR":"Job.2.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.2.3","value":"Job.2.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.5.17-18","r":"Job.5.17-18","rawR":"Job.5.17-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.5.17-18","value":"Job.5.17-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:17-18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.19.25-27","r":"Job.19.25-27","rawR":"Job.19.25-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.19.25-27","value":"Job.19.25-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:25-27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.33.15-28","r":"Job.33.15-28","rawR":"Job.33.15-28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.33.15-28","value":"Job.33.15-28"}],"t":"ref","v":"33:15-28"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.36.8-15","r":"Job.36.8-15","rawR":"Job.36.8-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.36.8-15","value":"Job.36.8-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"36:8-15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.38.2","r":"Job.38.2","rawR":"Job.38.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.38.2","value":"Job.38.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"38:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.40.8","r":"Job.40.8","rawR":"Job.40.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.40.8","value":"Job.40.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"40:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.42.7","r":"Job.42.7","rawR":"Job.42.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.42.7","value":"Job.42.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Pr.3.11","r":"Pr.3.11","rawR":"Pr.3.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.3.11","value":"Pr.3.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prov 3:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.12.7","r":"Heb.12.7","rawR":"Heb.12.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.12.7","value":"Heb.12.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 12:7"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.12.10","r":"Heb.12.10","rawR":"Heb.12.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.12.10","value":"Heb.12.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jas.5.11","r":"Jas.5.11","rawR":"Jas.5.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jas.5.11","value":"Jas.5.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jas 5:11"}],"sourceClass":"theme-refs","t":"p"}],"id":"ThemeNote:UnderstandingJob","refs":[{"book":"JOB","endChapter":42,"endVerse":17,"startChapter":38,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"UnderstandingJob","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"ThemeNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"JOB","sourceChapterCoverage":[38,39,40,41,42],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5ca39c43e11da8de13a2a430f8b5cd8f60e873839923ba2070e996921f8e26bd","sourceItemName":"UnderstandingJob","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/ThemeNotes.xml","sourceOrder":106,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"JOB","canonicalOSIS":"Job","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Job"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Job.38.1-42.17","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":"Understanding Job","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Understanding Job","type":"ThemeNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Job.41.1","r":"Job.41.1","rawR":"Job.41.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.41.1","value":"Job.41.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"41:1"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," Unlike the peaceful Behemoth (",{"href":"?bref=Job.40.15-24","r":"Job.40.15-24","rawR":"Job.40.15-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.40.15-24","value":"Job.40.15-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"40:15-24"},"), ",{"c":["Leviathan"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," was menacing (see also ",{"href":"?bref=Job.3.8","r":"Job.3.8","rawR":"Job.3.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.3.8","value":"Job.3.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.74.14","r":"Ps.74.14","rawR":"Ps.74.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.74.14","value":"Ps.74.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 74:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.104.26","r":"Ps.104.26","rawR":"Ps.104.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.104.26","value":"Ps.104.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"104:26"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.27.1","r":"Isa.27.1","rawR":"Isa.27.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.27.1","value":"Isa.27.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isa 27:1"},"). Most commentators identify Leviathan with the crocodile, with its terrible jaws (",{"href":"?bref=Job.41.14","r":"Job.41.14","rawR":"Job.41.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.41.14","value":"Job.41.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Job 41:14"},") and armored hide (",{"href":"?bref=Job.41.15-17","r":"Job.41.15-17","rawR":"Job.41.15-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.41.15-17","value":"Job.41.15-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"41:15-17"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Job.41.23","r":"Job.41.23","rawR":"Job.41.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.41.23","value":"Job.41.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"23"},"), thrashing the water (",{"href":"?bref=Job.41.31-32","r":"Job.41.31-32","rawR":"Job.41.31-32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.41.31-32","value":"Job.41.31-32"}],"t":"ref","v":"41:31-32"},"). But Leviathan is a fire-breathing dragon (",{"href":"?bref=Job.41.18-21","r":"Job.41.18-21","rawR":"Job.41.18-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.41.18-21","value":"Job.41.18-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"41:18-21"},") that wraps its coils around the sun to cause an eclipse (",{"href":"?bref=Job.3.8-9","r":"Job.3.8-9","rawR":"Job.3.8-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.3.8-9","value":"Job.3.8-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:8-9"},"). The background for Leviathan is the seven-headed sea monster that represents chaos in ancient Near Eastern mythology. In the biblical record, this unruly maritime monster is a frequent biblical image for chaos and wickedness, whose head the Lord crushes (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.74.14","r":"Ps.74.14","rawR":"Ps.74.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.74.14","value":"Ps.74.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 74:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.27.1","r":"Isa.27.1","rawR":"Isa.27.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.27.1","value":"Isa.27.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isa 27:1"},"; cp. ",{"href":"?bref=Job.9.13","r":"Job.9.13","rawR":"Job.9.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.9.13","value":"Job.9.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Job 9:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.26.12","r":"Job.26.12","rawR":"Job.26.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.26.12","value":"Job.26.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.89.9-10","r":"Ps.89.9-10","rawR":"Ps.89.9-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.89.9-10","value":"Ps.89.9-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 89:9-10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.30.7","r":"Isa.30.7","rawR":"Isa.30.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.30.7","value":"Isa.30.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isa 30:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.51.9","r":"Isa.51.9","rawR":"Isa.51.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.51.9","value":"Isa.51.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"51:9"},"). Later in the Bible, Satan is linked to the ancient serpent (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.3.1-24","r":"Gen.3.1-24","rawR":"Gen.3.1-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.3.1-24","value":"Gen.3.1-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gen 3"},") and unruly dragon (",{"href":"?bref=Rev.12.9","r":"Rev.12.9","rawR":"Rev.12.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.12.9","value":"Rev.12.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rev 12:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.20.2","r":"Rev.20.2","rawR":"Rev.20.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.20.2","value":"Rev.20.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"20:2"},"), whose head Christ and his followers crush (",{"href":"?bref=Rom.16.20","r":"Rom.16.20","rawR":"Rom.16.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.16.20","value":"Rom.16.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 16:20"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Job.41.1","refs":[{"book":"JOB","endChapter":41,"endVerse":1,"startChapter":41,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Job.41.1","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"JOB","sourceChapterCoverage":[41],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3a763c6bdf58439d41c8af9a27e5e43d50a7865ce8a9e1781aaab52d56c30e60","sourceItemName":"Job.41.1","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":5944,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"JOB","canonicalOSIS":"Job","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Job"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Job.41.1","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Job.41.1","type":"StudyNote"}],"version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}